# Balam Rush Heliux Pro HEX75 CPU cooler display controller.
#
# usb.ids mislabels this device as an "MSR-101U magnetic card reader"; it is a
# no-name microcontroller exposing a vendor-defined 64-byte HID pipe. See
# a cloned ID also used by USB relay boards.
#
# Without this, its /dev/hidraw node is root-only (crw------- root root) and
# mimarchy cannot write display frames.
#
# TAG+="uaccess" is the tidier mechanism (session-scoped ACL, as the AURA
# controller gets), but logind only applies that ACL on a real device-add, so
# it does not take effect on `udevadm trigger` and left the node unreadable
# here. GROUP/MODE applies immediately and unconditionally, so both are set:
# uaccess for a clean boot-time path, group ownership as the one that reliably
# works. `input` is used because the account is already a member; no new group
# and no world-writable node.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="5131", ATTRS{idProduct}=="2007", \
    TAG+="uaccess", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
